1
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,480
Move closer together.

2
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:47,680
You're out of the frame.

3
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,400
A little closer!

4
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,240
Three.

5
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:10,960
Two.

6
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,080
One.

7
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,240
Let me see it.

8
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:23,680
See what?

9
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,320
- The photo.
- Five hundred.

10
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:32,080
Four hundred. That's my final offer.

11
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:35,200
Or if you treat me to a meal,
I might consider it.

12
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:38,040
Say something, will you?

13
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:41,360
Or you can offer something else!

14
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,640
Yanzhou!

15
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:01,800
JI HENG HOSPITAL OF QINGYI CITY

16
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:23,240
Your sister isn't here today.

17
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:26,840
Didn't you tell her you were coming today?

18
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:28,040
No.

19
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,280
We haven't been in touch for a while.

20
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,240
Did you two fight?

21
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:48,640
You're siblings.
It's normal to fight sometimes.

22
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,360
My sister…

23
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:52,720
What has she been up to lately?

24
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:55,800
Recently, she took on a new tutoring gig.

25
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,640
She seems to get along
pretty well with the girl.

26
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:04,000
The girl kept pestering your sister
to take her out somewhere.

27
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,840
And your sister actually agreed.

28
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:07,720
In the past,

29
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,080
how could that ever happen?

30
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,440
They're going out?

31
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,680
Yes. I think they're going to the beach.

32
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,560
Are you jealous
that your sister gets to go out?

33
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,760
I'm jealous of that girl.

34
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,680
You don't need to envy anyone.

35
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:31,880
Open the drawer next to you.

36
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,520
There's a piece of paper inside.

37
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:36,280
Your sister left something for you.

38
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,160
This?

39
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,280
BOOK LIST FOR SCHOOL

40
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:58,520
SIS, HAPPY LUNAR NEW YEAR
XIAOMIAN

41
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:09,240
BOOK LIST FOR SCHOOL
1. MUST-BUY, 2. FOR REFERENCE

42
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,560
SAVE

43
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,800
WANG SIYUN: BEGINNING OF SPRING

44
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,080
LIKED BY XU FANGLI,
ZHUANG NING, ZHANG QI, LIU LINLIN

45
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,040
<i>Where is this?</i>

46
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,920
<i>Isn't this your Moments cover photo?</i>

47
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,680
<i>Did you go on a trip?</i>

48
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:35,640
I won't like the post.

49
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:38,920
What?

50
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:42,240
After all, I'm not even in the photo.

51
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,560
CHEN HUIMEI

52
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:54,400
Oh no.

53
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:05,520
- Hello?
- <i>How's it going? Are you having fun?</i>

54
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:09,320
How did you know I went out?

55
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:10,560
<i>Ms. Xiaozheng told me.</i>

56
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:13,640
<i>She said you've been doing great</i>
<i>and told me to reward you.</i>

57
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,840
And here I was foolishly
sending you photos of me studying.

58
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:20,160
<i>I was really happy</i>
<i>that you sent me photos, okay?</i>

59
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:23,160
<i>Go ahead and have fun.</i>
<i>I won't disturb you.</i>

60
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:26,160
You good? Is everything okay?

61
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:30,520
You told Chen Huimei we were going out?

62
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:34,920
Would I really just do what you suggested
and get paid for doing nothing?

63
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:38,600
Thank you.

64
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,800
You're thanking me too early.

65
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:43,880
Here.

66
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:50,880
I made a reading list for you.

67
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:54,080
The study materials on the market
are a mixed bag.

68
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,280
You can use this for reference.

69
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:58,200
We're out having fun.
Don't be such a buzzkill.

70
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:04,320
You bought so many reference books
just to research this for me?

71
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:07,600
I didn't buy them.
I read them at the bookstore.

72
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,680
Next year, my younger brother
will take the College Entrance Exam too.

73
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:12,520
I'm helping him prep his study materials.

74
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,880
While I was at it,
I took a look for you too.

75
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:18,880
No wonder there were
exam questions in there.

76
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:22,480
Looks like your brother isn't very capable

77
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,040
if he needs you to do all this for him.

78
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,400
Don't be so hard on yourself.

79
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:28,160
I never asked you to prepare anything.

80
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:39,880
BOOK LIST FOR SCHOOL
1. MUST-BUY, 2. FOR REFERENCE

81
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:59,400
- ENJOYING A FEAST WITH THE FAMILY!
- LEARNING NEVER ENDS

82
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,760
<i>It's her.</i>

83
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:12,520
<i>Recently, she took on a new tutoring gig.</i>

84
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:15,440
<i>She seems to get along</i>
<i>pretty well with the girl.</i>

85
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:34,880
TUTORING CONTRACT RENEWAL AGREEMENT

86
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,799
This…

87
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,640
Winter break is too short.

88
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:41,480
I feel like I barely learned anything.

89
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:45,320
So I discussed it with Chen Huimei,

90
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,440
and we're planning
to extend the tutoring sessions.

91
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:50,360
You'd better keep working hard.

92
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,280
I'm aiming for the top 30.

93
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,000
- In your class?
- In my grade!

94
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:02,320
Gao Xing.

95
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,000
Thank you.

96
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:10,200
Don't get the wrong idea.
It's not that I approve of you.

97
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:13,800
This is just a fair exchange.

98
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:15,360
What's a fair exchange?

99
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,520
You know what I mean.

100
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:30,720
Gao Xing renewed
her tutoring sessions with me.

101
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:32,280
How about I buy you a drink too?

102
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:56,240
What's in your backpack?
It's stuffed!

103
00:09:57,160 --> 00:09:58,040
Books.

104
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:01,000
I didn't see you bring
many books home over break.

105
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,440
Why is your bag so full now?

106
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:11,720
My tutor gave me a reading list.
I bought every book on it.

107
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:13,080
What kind of tutor works miracles?

108
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:14,760
- Let me see.
- No way.

109
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:16,000
There are only two copies.

110
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:17,800
So technically,
I'm the only one who has one.

111
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:25,040
Acting cool again.

112
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:29,680
Did I say that out loud?

113
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:31,600
I'm not deaf.

114
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,400
Jiang Mian.

115
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,560
I was saying you looked cool.
You should be happy.

116
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:48,600
GUO XIAO

117
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,800
<i>I transferred the perfume money</i>
<i>to your bank account.</i>

118
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,120
<i>Check whether it came through.</i>

119
00:10:57,360 --> 00:11:00,120
<i>Got it. I just spent all</i>
<i>my Lunar New Year money,</i>

120
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,520
<i>so this came at the perfect time.</i>

121
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:06,680
WU FA

122
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:11,840
<i>Money's received.</i>
<i>Looks like there's always a way after all.</i>

123
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,840
They still haven't
returned from their trip?

124
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:33,120
They missed their flight,
so they rebooked.

125
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:35,360
They probably won't
get back until late tonight.

126
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,400
Where are you going so late?

127
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,480
Fangli just texted me saying

128
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:15,160
she and Linlin got locked out
of the dorm building.

129
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:18,320
If they wake up the staff to let them in,
they'll be marked as returning late.

130
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:21,680
They will lose points
and have to write a statement of apology.

131
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:48,680
What do we do?

132
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:07,400
PLEASE RING THE DOORBELL

133
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:24,600
LIYUAN BUILDING 9

134
00:13:58,400 --> 00:13:59,560
Zheng Yu.

135
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:03,360
Ma'am, the clothes I hung
on the balcony fell downstairs.

136
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,960
Wait, why aren't you asleep?

137
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:07,600
Why are you out on the balcony
hanging up clothes at this hour?

138
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,040
I forgot to wash them earlier.

139
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,960
We have field practice
in the mountains tomorrow.

140
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:12,760
And it's my only jacket.

141
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,720
Then…

142
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,280
Go get it.

143
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:28,200
It's too dark outside.

144
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:29,440
I can barely see anything.

145
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,680
Fine, wait a moment.

146
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,480
Let's go.

147
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:17,120
None of us brought our keys.

148
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:29,640
The dorm supervisor is making
her rounds! Hurry up!

149
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,760
Zhuang Ning,
why is your collarbone sitting so high?

150
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:48,360
No, no. Don't move.

151
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:04,120
That scared me.

152
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,840
Zheng Yu, thank goodness you were there.

153
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:10,880
And Zhuang Ning too.

154
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:12,880
We have Zheng Yu to thank.

155
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:15,880
Thank you.

156
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:24,040
We should get some rest.

157
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,560
We'll be heading
into the mountains in just a few hours.

158
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,240
Right.

159
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:33,480
Get up.

160
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,360
Everyone, hurry and get on the bus!

161
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,600
Once you're on,
check in with your group members

162
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,640
to make sure everyone's here.

163
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:45,680
The group list is in the group chat.

164
00:16:56,360 --> 00:17:00,120
Where are you sitting, Zheng Yu?
Why aren't you moving?

165
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:01,960
Everyone's waiting to get on.

166
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,160
Zheng Yu.

167
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:18,880
We were put in the same group
and are sharing a room.

168
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:21,400
Can I sit here?

169
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:25,359
It's fine.

170
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:31,240
Zheng Yu, want some coffee?

171
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:33,160
It's okay. Thank you. You drink it.

172
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:36,360
Fangli and Linlin bought them for us.

173
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:37,840
We were up so late last night.

174
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,360
This should help you stay awake.

175
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:53,560
WEST S385

176
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,240
The coffee isn't working.

177
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:10,680
I want to get some sun.

178
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:02,720
Don't forget to take it.

179
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:05,680
Did you leave the water bottle on the bus?

180
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:07,960
Give me your luggage.

181
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:12,680
Everyone, gather around for a moment.
I have a few things to say.

182
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:15,640
Last summer, the training base
was under maintenance,

183
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:17,440
so our field practice had to be postponed.

184
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:19,680
This year, we're finally doing it.

185
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:23,520
The most important thing
during field practice is to stay safe.

186
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:25,040
Don't leave the group on your own.

187
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,800
Take all necessary safety precautions.

188
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:29,360
At the same time,
you must complete your assignments

189
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,880
and apply what you've learned
in the classroom

190
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,520
to your practical work.

191
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:36,120
Zhang Qi, hand out
these logbooks to everyone.

192
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Make sure you take good care
of the logbook you receive.

193
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:42,640
You must fill it out every day.

194
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:45,240
We'll inspect them
after the training ends.

195
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:48,040
Every activity
will be assessed and graded.

196
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:49,800
Has everyone received a logbook?

197
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,640
- Yes!
- Yes!

198
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:53,600
Now, go to the front desk
for your room keys.

199
00:19:53,680 --> 00:19:56,240
Drop off your luggage,
then get yourselves settled.

200
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,120
We'll gather at the entrance
at ten o'clock.

201
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:00,280
- We'll head into the mountains then.
- Okay!

202
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:01,200
Okay, let's go!

203
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:03,080
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

204
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:05,160
- Do you want to stay together?
- Let's stay together.

205
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,640
Let's stay together.

206
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,040
Is your bag heavy?

207
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:14,320
Why don't you put it on my suitcase?
It'll be easier for you.

208
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:15,960
It's fine. I can manage.

209
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:17,120
Let's go.

210
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,720
- It's fine.
- I'll carry it.

211
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:21,720
It's okay.

212
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,280
Yanzhou.

213
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:25,800
Should I go over and give a heads-up?

214
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:30,120
Heads-up about what?
And to whom?

215
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,480
I snore when I sleep.

216
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:34,920
If that bothers you,
I'll let the group leader know

217
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,240
and switch rooms with someone.

218
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:38,200
I don't mind.

219
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,080
Then you're in for a rough night.

220
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:49,840
You don't even belong in this room.

221
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:51,200
Why are you hanging around here?

222
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:55,320
Xie Yudi has our room keycard,
and I can't find him.

223
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,600
You're pretty close to Xie Yudi.

224
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:04,200
Just between us, does he like Zheng Yu?

225
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:11,000
Why else would he always help her out?

226
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:14,080
He donated for her last time,
and just now he was carrying her bag.

227
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:15,360
It's been three years.

228
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,440
Everyone in class knows.

229
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:19,320
You, the class monitor,
are probably the last one to find out.

230
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:20,880
Tell me more.

231
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,960
- Drop it.
- Come on, tell me!

232
00:21:24,760 --> 00:21:28,080
Hotels these days aren't always safe.

233
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:30,560
Even in places like this,
there could be hidden cameras.

234
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:31,880
We should check.

235
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:40,080
I'm staying here for Zhuang Ning.

236
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,640
You mightn't know,
but we went to high school together.

237
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:45,200
Back then, she was often bullied.

238
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:46,760
Our families are close,

239
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:49,680
so during the New Year break,
Uncle Zhuang asked me to look after her.

240
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,520
You can ask her if you don't believe me.

241
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:01,720
We really were high school classmates.

242
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:06,040
I ran into Xie Yudi downstairs just now.

243
00:22:06,120 --> 00:22:09,000
He said he would keep waiting for you.

244
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:11,600
If you don't see him,
he might keep sending people.

245
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:13,960
<i>Then the whole building will know.</i>

246
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:23,480
Xie Yudi. I don't need
any more help from you here.

247
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:24,960
You can leave.

248
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,680
Okay.

249
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:42,760
Xie Yudi always used to know
where I was in the past.

250
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,200
You were the one telling him, right?

251
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:47,520
I don't like that.

252
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:58,760
When observing and documenting plants,

253
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:00,760
be sure to record the observation date,

254
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:03,120
including the exact month and day.

255
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:06,160
You also need to record the latitude,
longitude, and elevation.

256
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:09,080
From a broad overview to fine details,
there are four sections in total.

257
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:11,040
I see many of you brought cameras too.

258
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:13,840
When you photograph the plants later,
remember this.

259
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:15,520
Don't just photograph one plant.

260
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:17,120
Photograph the entire cluster.

261
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:19,280
Document the shape
of the branches and their color.

262
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:22,280
Next are the leaves.
Pay close attention to them.

263
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:23,840
Photograph both sides,

264
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:26,720
and touch the leaves
to feel their texture.

265
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:28,360
Be sure to record that too.

266
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:29,920
Finally, the flowers and fruit.

267
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,920
That will give you
a complete record of the plant.

268
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:34,360
Let me see yours.

269
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:39,200
STORAGE FULL

270
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:43,760
Zheng Yu, use this.

271
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:48,120
It's okay. I'll just clear some space.

272
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:51,880
Take plenty of photos.

273
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:54,360
We can use your photos
for the presentation later.

274
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:56,920
Okay.

275
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:02,680
DELETE THESE ITEMS?

276
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:18,920
What's on your mind?

277
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:22,240
Everyone, listen up.

278
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:23,800
There's a pavilion up ahead.

279
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:26,720
We'll go there and take a 30-minute break.
Drink some water and grab a bite.

280
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:28,680
Later, we'll form groups
to set up sample plots.

281
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:30,160
- Okay.
- Okay.

282
00:24:30,240 --> 00:24:33,120
- Let's go.
- Let's gather.

283
00:24:57,040 --> 00:24:58,920
Chen Yanzhou, she's over there.

284
00:25:29,720 --> 00:25:30,960
Xie Yudi.

285
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:11,680
This is your hat, right?

286
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:14,960
Why did it end up with me?

287
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:18,680
It got windy earlier,
and my hat blew away.

288
00:26:18,760 --> 00:26:20,920
It probably blew it right onto your face.

289
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:24,000
You should be happy.

290
00:26:24,080 --> 00:26:26,200
It takes sharp features
for it to stay put.

291
00:26:42,960 --> 00:26:44,320
It's all my fault.

292
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:45,560
I have terrible luck.

293
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:47,960
I drew the highest spot
for our sample plot.

294
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:49,960
It's not too bad.

295
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:51,400
The slope isn't very steep.

296
00:26:56,360 --> 00:26:58,760
Be careful.
Those shoes can slip easily.

297
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:36,520
I used to think
you just didn't like to smile.

298
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:10,720
- What is it?
- Nothing.

299
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,520
I just feel like

300
00:28:12,600 --> 00:28:15,280
since winter ended,
you've seemed a little different.

301
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:24,800
Back in high school,

302
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:28,560
I used to love putting all kinds of
motivational stickers on my laptop too.

303
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:30,840
Were stickers popular back then
where you were too?

304
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:33,240
I didn't have a laptop in high school.

305
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:35,200
I bought this for cheap

306
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:38,520
on the Campus Forum
when I started university.

307
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:10,520
THIS PLACE HAS TOO MANY MOSQUITOES.

308
00:29:10,600 --> 00:29:11,960
GO BUY SOME MOSQUITO REPELLENT.

309
00:29:20,520 --> 00:29:22,320
I bought fresh strawberries
from the locals.

310
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:23,280
They're washed.

311
00:29:25,120 --> 00:29:26,160
I'll get going.

312
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:34,040
Zheng Yu, have some strawberries.

313
00:29:35,760 --> 00:29:37,160
I already brushed my teeth.

314
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:42,000
Where are you going so late?

315
00:29:43,760 --> 00:29:44,880
I need some fresh air.

316
00:29:55,480 --> 00:29:57,200
BOTANICAL INFORMATION

317
00:30:01,680 --> 00:30:04,000
Bougainvillea.

318
00:30:04,080 --> 00:30:05,600
Black nightshade.

319
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,160
And…

320
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:09,440
This is--

321
00:30:09,520 --> 00:30:11,480
Hairy maiden fern
from the <i>Thelypteridaceae </i>family.

322
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:13,400
It's a perennial herb.

323
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:15,880
No need to count them.
We have enough. Let me carry these.

324
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:18,840
It's fine. I've got it.

325
00:30:18,920 --> 00:30:22,120
You guys found most of these,

326
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:23,800
so I should help out somehow.

327
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:30,120
Should we find an open area tonight
and try light trapping?

328
00:30:31,520 --> 00:30:34,160
Isn't it too early in the season
for light trapping?

329
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:36,280
Besides, we don't have the equipment.

330
00:30:36,360 --> 00:30:37,720
We're already here.

331
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:40,000
If we find anything,
we might even earn extra points.

332
00:30:40,080 --> 00:30:42,240
As for the equipment,
I'll take care of it.

333
00:30:42,880 --> 00:30:44,000
What do you think?

334
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:45,880
I… I don't mind.

335
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:56,520
Zhuang Ning, aren't you going to eat?

336
00:30:57,280 --> 00:30:58,360
I'm not that hungry.

337
00:30:58,440 --> 00:31:00,800
I want to prepare the materials
for this afternoon's specimens.

338
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:22,600
There are so many empty seats.
You're not cramped here?

339
00:31:23,560 --> 00:31:27,240
The teacher said that members of
the same group should stick together.

340
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:38,440
<i>I don't remember this being</i>
<i>part of your field practice schedule.</i>

341
00:31:40,320 --> 00:31:41,200
Are you done eating?

342
00:31:48,080 --> 00:31:49,400
<i>Say hello to the boss for me.</i>

343
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:02,560
<i>I remember a guy from last year's class</i>

344
00:32:02,640 --> 00:32:05,720
<i>who used light trapping as an excuse</i>
<i>to take his girlfriend stargazing.</i>

345
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:08,360
<i>She ended up getting bitten by bugs,</i>

346
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:10,120
<i>and she dumped him when they got back.</i>

347
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:12,880
<i>Remember to bring some ointment.</i>

348
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:18,680
Weren't you done eating?

349
00:32:22,520 --> 00:32:23,680
I'm hungry again.

350
00:32:25,600 --> 00:32:26,720
So childish.

351
00:32:42,840 --> 00:32:46,880
The kitchen staff said they'd never
seen a plate scraped so clean.

352
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:48,520
They gave us another plate for free.

353
00:32:49,720 --> 00:32:51,960
Weren't you hungry again?
Eat some more.

354
00:34:02,560 --> 00:34:04,280
I WOKE UP LATE
AND DIDN'T GO UP THE MOUNTAIN.

355
00:34:04,360 --> 00:34:05,720
GIVE ME SOME OF YOUR SAMPLES.

356
00:34:38,560 --> 00:34:40,360
- What's wrong?
- Several species are missing.

357
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:48,120
I think this was all I had
when I brought them back.

358
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:52,440
Could you have dropped some
on the way back to base?

359
00:34:53,679 --> 00:34:54,679
That's possible.

360
00:34:54,760 --> 00:34:56,199
I wasn't paying much attention.

361
00:34:57,560 --> 00:34:58,880
Never mind. This should be enough.

362
00:34:58,960 --> 00:35:00,000
Let's finish these first.

363
00:35:10,280 --> 00:35:11,680
I'm going to the restroom.

364
00:35:14,840 --> 00:35:17,280
Hey, don't mess with me. Go away!

365
00:35:53,840 --> 00:35:55,040
Zhuang Ning.

366
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:58,000
It's about time to go light trapping.

367
00:35:58,080 --> 00:36:00,640
I… I have a bit of diarrhea.

368
00:36:00,720 --> 00:36:02,560
I'd like to stay here and rest.

369
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:04,240
Is it bad?

370
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:06,800
It's fine. It happens all the time.

371
00:36:06,880 --> 00:36:10,560
I have a sensitive stomach. I often
get diarrhea if I get a bit of a cold.

372
00:36:10,640 --> 00:36:12,640
Then get some rest. I'll head out first.

373
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:36,480
THE FOOD IN THIS PLACE IS AWFUL.
GO GET ME SOME TAKEOUT.

374
00:36:36,560 --> 00:36:38,000
I'LL WAIT FOR YOU IN THE ACTIVITY ROOM.

375
00:36:40,800 --> 00:36:42,000
<i>Starting navigation.</i>

376
00:36:42,080 --> 00:36:43,200
<i>The total distance is 2 km.</i>

377
00:36:43,280 --> 00:36:45,240
<i>You'll arrive at 8:20 p.m.</i>

378
00:36:45,320 --> 00:36:46,320
<i>Depart now.</i>

379
00:36:46,400 --> 00:36:48,360
<i>Turn right in 214 m.</i>

380
00:37:02,560 --> 00:37:05,280
ACADEMIC BUILDING

381
00:37:11,120 --> 00:37:12,920
Something came up,
so Zhuang Ning can't make it.

382
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:16,000
Where did you get all this stuff?

383
00:37:17,160 --> 00:37:19,120
I heard Li Yanan mention before

384
00:37:19,200 --> 00:37:21,400
that the base owner
is an insect enthusiast,

385
00:37:21,480 --> 00:37:22,920
so I borrowed some equipment from him.

386
00:37:24,680 --> 00:37:25,800
Let's go.

387
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:55,360
Let's set it up here.

388
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:39,640
Guess how many insect species
will land here tonight.

389
00:38:39,720 --> 00:38:41,680
It's only early spring.

390
00:38:41,760 --> 00:38:44,200
Light trapping is best done in May
or June at the earliest.

391
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:47,360
Well, let's see.

392
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:57,560
Indian owlet-moth.

393
00:38:58,600 --> 00:39:00,040
Silver-striped hawkmoth.

394
00:39:00,720 --> 00:39:01,880
Geometrid moth.

395
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:03,720
Japanese vine hawkmoth.

396
00:39:04,480 --> 00:39:05,360
Cotton bollworm.

397
00:39:07,040 --> 00:39:08,360
You have great eyesight.

398
00:39:09,360 --> 00:39:10,560
So do you.

399
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:15,000
I first learned that insects
are attracted to light

400
00:39:15,080 --> 00:39:16,920
when I was in my second year
of elementary school.

401
00:39:18,080 --> 00:39:19,440
Then you're smarter than me.

402
00:39:21,360 --> 00:39:22,640
My older brother told me.

403
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:33,920
He said living things instinctively move
toward goals they can see clearly.

404
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:37,000
I found him so annoying back then

405
00:39:37,080 --> 00:39:38,520
because he was the kind of person

406
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:41,000
who saw goals clearly
and could move toward them effortlessly.

407
00:39:44,520 --> 00:39:46,840
He was also the one who took me
light trapping for the first time.

408
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:50,160
I'd never seen so many
nasty bugs in my life.

409
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:56,160
Why did you choose this major?

410
00:39:58,240 --> 00:39:59,440
My reason is pretty boring.

411
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:02,760
I won a biology competition
when I was in high school,

412
00:40:02,840 --> 00:40:04,720
so I got an early admission
to Qing Yi University.

413
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:07,800
I considered switching majors to study
something more profitable,

414
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:10,120
but this is Qing Yi University's
best major,

415
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:12,720
and I could compete
for the Vitality Award.

416
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:14,880
After considering it, I decided to stay.

417
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:22,000
Hey, look. There are so many!

418
00:40:36,080 --> 00:40:39,080
Let's photograph all these insects and
include them in the Field Practice Report.

419
00:40:40,120 --> 00:40:42,720
Then could you do
the presentation slides this time?

420
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:47,760
Then you take the photos.

421
00:42:42,960 --> 00:42:44,560
The food's still hot.

422
00:42:44,640 --> 00:42:45,600
I'll get going.

423
00:42:45,680 --> 00:42:46,560
What's the rush?

424
00:42:49,040 --> 00:42:52,680
Our group agreed to go light trapping
together, and I'm already late.

425
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:57,120
Zheng Yu and that repeating student
have already left?

426
00:42:58,680 --> 00:43:00,320
What's the deal with those two?

427
00:43:01,320 --> 00:43:03,200
I… I'm not sure.

428
00:43:04,760 --> 00:43:05,800
Why are you nervous?

429
00:43:10,840 --> 00:43:12,280
Your roommate is so pretty.

430
00:43:13,280 --> 00:43:15,200
It's normal that
she has a few guys around her.

431
00:43:16,640 --> 00:43:17,760
But

432
00:43:19,080 --> 00:43:21,480
it's a bit weird to always hang out

433
00:43:22,480 --> 00:43:24,440
with the same person, isn't it?

434
00:43:27,240 --> 00:43:28,440
Like the two of us.

435
00:43:29,800 --> 00:43:30,840
Do you think

436
00:43:31,840 --> 00:43:32,760
that's normal?

437
00:43:38,840 --> 00:43:39,840
Hard to answer?

438
00:43:43,240 --> 00:43:44,520
Let me ask you something else.

439
00:43:48,440 --> 00:43:50,800
Zheng Yu likes Chen Yanzhou.

440
00:43:52,440 --> 00:43:53,680
Are they dating?

441
00:43:56,560 --> 00:43:57,520
I don't know.

442
00:44:01,840 --> 00:44:03,320
Aren't you two roommates?

443
00:44:04,440 --> 00:44:05,880
How do you know nothing?

444
00:44:11,720 --> 00:44:12,720
Then tell me.

445
00:44:14,080 --> 00:44:14,920
What do you know?

446
00:44:16,880 --> 00:44:18,000
She doesn't like you.

447
00:44:43,640 --> 00:44:45,400
You know I've been
pretty nice to you, right?

448
00:44:47,800 --> 00:44:50,240
Compared to before,
you've definitely toned it down.

449
00:44:52,720 --> 00:44:53,720
Of course.

450
00:44:55,200 --> 00:44:56,880
We're adults now, after all.

451
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:01,640
Your phone.

452
00:45:10,680 --> 00:45:11,520
Let me borrow it.

453
00:45:12,360 --> 00:45:13,440
Thanks.

454
00:45:40,400 --> 00:45:41,440
Thank you.

455
00:45:41,520 --> 00:45:42,680
I found what I lost.

456
00:46:24,760 --> 00:46:25,960
I'll return the equipment.

457
00:46:27,960 --> 00:46:29,360
In that case, I'll head back to my room.

458
00:46:46,960 --> 00:46:48,960
Excuse me. Do you have any
antidiarrheal medicine?

459
00:46:49,040 --> 00:46:50,640
Something for an upset stomach
from a cold.

460
00:46:51,240 --> 00:46:52,600
Just a moment. Let me check.

461
00:47:01,840 --> 00:47:03,040
Zhuang Ning.

462
00:47:04,000 --> 00:47:04,920
Zhuang Ning.

463
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:29,160
NEW MESSAGE

464
00:47:35,400 --> 00:47:36,760
<i>There's a campground nearby.</i>

465
00:47:36,840 --> 00:47:39,160
<i>I'll wait for you there.</i>
<i>There's something I need to tell you.</i>

466
00:50:11,560 --> 00:50:16,560
Subtitle translation by: Cempaka Malinja
